From: ImmortalWrt ECM30 bring-up <ecm30@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] serial: 8250: retain the platform's no-TEMT-IRQ capability

dw8250_setup_port() declares UART_CAP_NOTEMT before registering the port.
On T113 the component parameter register is unavailable, so the port type
is subsequently probed by autoconfig(). That resets the capabilities to
the generic 16550A table and loses UART_CAP_NOTEMT.

The software RS485 stop path then waits for a TEMT interrupt which this
UART does not generate. GPIO RTS remains asserted after the first send,
preventing the opposite port from replying. Retain the driver's explicit
timing capability across type detection so the existing 8250 frame timer
deasserts RTS after the final byte. Keep normal FIFO/type probing intact.

--- a/drivers/tty/serial/8250/8250_port.c
+++ b/drivers/tty/serial/8250/8250_port.c
@@ -3157,6 +3157,7 @@ static void serial8250_config_port(struct
 {
 	struct uart_8250_port *up = up_to_u8250p(port);
+	unsigned int no_temt_irq = up->capabilities & UART_CAP_NOTEMT;
 	int ret;
 
 	/*
@@ -3173,6 +3174,9 @@ static void serial8250_config_port(struct
 	if (flags & UART_CONFIG_TYPE)
 		autoconfig(up);
 
+	/* Type detection cannot discover the platform's missing TEMT IRQ. */
+	up->capabilities |= no_temt_irq;
+
 	/* HW bugs may trigger IRQ while IIR == NO_INT */
 	if (port->type == PORT_TEGRA)
 		up->bugs |= UART_BUG_NOMSR;
